      "content": "Deload weeks or reducing volume can help alleviate plateaus by giving your client's muscles time to recover and rebuild from the repetitive stress of the squat. By temporarily scaling back the intensity or frequency of squat workouts, you can replenish energy stores, recover imbalances, and allow the nervous system to adapt. This can lead to a boost in strength and subsequent progress. Additionally, reducing volume can also help identify and exacerbate any underlying weaknesses or issues that may be hindering progress.",
